# Counter staff: any trader, and the Lupercal's three by name (their voices are set in the vessel's WFCrewBarks).
# Said along with the common lines.

wf-crew-bark-trader-struck-1 = Ha! The Boss is in fine spirits today.
wf-crew-bark-trader-struck-2 = Thank you, Boss! Best customer I've got.
wf-crew-bark-trader-struck-3 = Boss! I'd put that on your tab, if you ever paid.

wf-crew-bark-trader-greet-boss-1 = Boss! Anything you need, on the house.
wf-crew-bark-trader-greet-boss-2 = The Boss! Counter's always open for you.

wf-crew-bark-trader-greet-guest-1 = Come on over, take a look.
wf-crew-bark-trader-greet-guest-2 = Prices are fair. Mostly. Have a browse.

wf-crew-bark-trader-idle-1 = Business is slow. The Boss scares the haggling out of everyone.
wf-crew-bark-trader-idle-2 = Counted the stock. Counted it again. Same number.
wf-crew-bark-trader-idle-3 = A customer! No. Just a draft.

# Torvald Deepkeel, the dockmaster.
wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-struck-1 = Felt that in me beard, Boss. Much obliged.
wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-struck-2 = Ha! Good arm on you, Boss.
wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-struck-3 = Thank you, Boss! Not been hit like that since the old yards.

wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-greet-boss-1 = Boss! Berths are full and the fees are paid.
wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-greet-boss-2 = Boss. Ring's running smooth as stone.

wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-greet-guest-1 = Need a berth? Talk to me at the desk.

wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-idle-1 = Berth three's clamps squeak. I'll get to it. Next century.
wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-idle-2 = Hundred and forty years of docking ships. Still love it.
wf-crew-bark-dockmaster-idle-3 = Somebody parked crooked again. Every shift.

# Imre Kast, the quartermaster.
wf-crew-bark-quartermaster-struck-1 = Thank you, Boss! I'll log that. Twice.
wf-crew-bark-quartermaster-struck-2 = Boss! Duly noted, duly counted.

wf-crew-bark-quartermaster-greet-boss-1 = Tanks are full, Boss. Counted them twice.

wf-crew-bark-quartermaster-greet-guest-1 = Need fuel? Got fuel.

wf-crew-bark-quartermaster-idle-1 = Forty litres... forty-one... no, forty. Start again.
wf-crew-bark-quartermaster-idle-2 = If the books balance, I sleep. They balance. I don't sleep.

# Agathe Lowe, the apothecary.
wf-crew-bark-apothecary-struck-1 = Oh! Thank you, dear. Er, Boss.
wf-crew-bark-apothecary-struck-2 = Goodness! Thank you, Boss, dear.
wf-crew-bark-apothecary-struck-3 = That'll want a poultice. Thank you, Boss!

wf-crew-bark-apothecary-greet-boss-1 = Hello, Boss, dear. Eat something green today.
wf-crew-bark-apothecary-greet-boss-2 = Boss! You look peaky, dear.

wf-crew-bark-apothecary-greet-staff-1 = Hello, { $name }, dear.

wf-crew-bark-apothecary-greet-guest-1 = Hello, dear. Bandages are on special.

wf-crew-bark-apothecary-idle-1 = Thirty years of pills and still nobody reads the label.
wf-crew-bark-apothecary-idle-2 = Somebody's coughing in the lobby. I can hear it from here.
wf-crew-bark-apothecary-idle-3 = Tea, a quiet counter, and nobody bleeding. Bliss.

wf-crew-bark-apothecary-healed-1 = Thank you, dear. I'd have done it neater, mind.
